        "code": "from soar.audit.log import record as audit_record\n\ndue = db.query(\n    \"SELECT id, execution_id, step_id, risk_level, action_key FROM approval \"\n    \"WHERE org_id = %s AND status = 'pending' AND expires_at < now()\",\n    [org_id], org_id,\n)\nfor approval in due:\n    db.execute(\n        \"UPDATE approval SET status = 'expired', decided_at = now() WHERE id = %s\",\n        [approval[\"id\"]], org_id,\n    )\n    audit_record(db, {\n        \"org_id\": org_id, \"actor_kind\": \"system\",\n        \"action\": \"approval.expired\", \"target_kind\": \"approval\",\n        \"target_id\": approval[\"id\"], \"execution_id\": approval.get(\"execution_id\"),\n        \"after\": {\"treated_as\": \"reject\"}, \"result\": \"success\",\n    })\nreturn due",
        "doc": "Expire approvals whose window has closed. A HIGH-risk approval that expires is always a rejection - the on_timeout \"proceed\" option does not exist for it, at the schema level and here.",
